## Why This Is Asked
Tests incremental counting, batch updates, and tight per-event amortized bounds, plus modulo-based pair counting with constant extra space.

## Key Concepts
- Residue class bookkeeping with O(1) per update
- Pair counting with modulo constraints
- Amortized vs worst-case trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
// insert/update logic
function apply(x, D, freq, total, op){
  const r = x % D;
  const idx = (D - r) % D;
  if(op==='insert'){ total += freq[idx]; freq[r]++; }
  else { freq[r]--; total -= freq[idx]; }
  return total;
}
```

